","The Fischer esterization reaction is a type of acid-catalyzed acid-acid coupling that produces an ester from a carboxylic acid and a alcohol. In summary, it is the oxidation of a carboxylic acid with a alcohol to form an ester and water. The reaction is named after Friedrich Fischer, who proposed it in 19-th century. The reaction is reversible, and the equilibrium is often shifted to favor the formation of the ester. 

