","The coefficient of friction (\(\mu\)) is dimensionless, meaning it does not have any physical units. This is because it is defined as the ratio of force of friction (\(F_f\)) to the normal force (\(F_n\)):  
\[
\mu = \frac{F_f}{F_n}
\]  
Since both \(F_f\) and \((\mu)\) are forces, they have the same units. Therefore, the coefficient of friction is dimensionless, and its dimensional representation is \([M^0 L^0 T^0]\).  

