   The surface is given by \(z = \sqrt{\frac{56 - x^2 - y^2}{9}}\).  
   The partial derivatives are:  
   \[
   \frac{\partial z}{\partial x} = -\frac{2x}{18\sqrt{56 - x^2 - y^2}} = -\frac{x}{9\sqrt{56 - x^2 - y^2}}
   \]  
   \[
   \frac{\partial z}{\partial y} = -\frac{2y}{18\sqrt{56 - x^2 - y^2}} = -\frac{y}{9\sqrt{56 - x^2 - y^2}}
   \]  
   The gradient of the surface is:  
   \[
   \nabla z = \left( \frac{\partial z}{\partial x}, \frac{\partial z}{\partial y}, \frac{\partial z}{\partial z} \right) = \left( -\frac{x}{9\sqrt{56 - x^2 - y^2}}, -\frac{y}{9\sqrt{56 - x^2 - y^2}}, 1 \right)
