   \[
   \frac{6000}{60 \text{ months}} = 100 \text{ month/year}
   \]

3. **Calculate the new monthly payment:**  
   \[
   100 \text{ month/year} + 150 = 250 \text{ month/year}
   \]

4. **Calculate the total number of months in the new plan:**  
   \[
   \frac{6000}{250 \text{ month/year}} = 24 \text{ minutes/year}
   \]

5. **Convert the new time period to years:**  
