The momentum transfer \( \Delta P \) is the difference between the initial and final momenta:
\[
\Delta P = P_f - P_i = (E_f/c, \mathbf{p}_f) - (E_i/c, \mathbf{p}_i) = \left( \frac{E_f - E_i}{c}, \mathbf{p}_f - \mathbf{p}_i \right).
\]
The square of the momentum transfer is:
\[
\Delta P^2 = \left( \frac{E_f - E_i}{c} \right)^2 + \left( \mathbf{p}_f - \mathbf{p}_i \right)^2.
\]
The square of the momentum transfer is equivalent to the square of the four-momentum transfer \( Q^2 \), which is:
\[
Q^2 = \Delta P^2 = \left( \frac{E_f - E_i}{c} \right)^2 + \left( \mathbf{p}_f - \mathbf{mathbf{p}}_i \right)^2.
\]
This is the expression for \( Q^2 \). 

Thus, the squared four-momentum transfer \( Q^2 \) is:
\[
Q^2 = \left( \frac{E_f - E_i}{c} \right)^2 + \left( \mathbf{p}_f - \mathbf{p}_i \right)^2.
\]",relevance,"# Task Description
