   \[
   Q_{\text{water}} = 1858.5 \text{ kJ/kg}
   \]
   The entropy change of the water is:
   \[
   S_{\text{water}} = \frac{Q_{\text{water}}}{T_{\text{water}}} = \frac{1858.5}{220} = 8.44 \text{ kJ/K}
   \]

3. **Total entropy change (\(S_{\text{total}}\))**:
   The total entropy change is the sum of the entropy changes of the gas and the water:
   \[
   S_{\text{total}} = S_{\text{gas}} + S_{\text{water}} = -0.484 m_{\text{gas}} + 8.44 \text{ kJ/K}
   \]

4. **Equating the heat transfer**:
   The heat lost by the gas equals the heat absorbed by the water:
   \[
   Q_{\text{gas}} = Q_{\text{water}} \implies 525.52 m_{\text{gas}} = 1858.5 \text{ kJ}
