   - Dark matter can lead to the gravitational collapse of gas clouds, which can trigger the formation of black holes. The presence of dark matter in the gas clouds increases their gravitational pull, which can lead to the formation of black holes.  
   - The presence of dark matter in the surrounding environment can lead to the growth of black holes through the accretion of nearby matter.  

3. Galaxy mergers and black hole mergers:  
