<start_of_turn>model
","The index of refraction (n) of a medium is defined as the ratio of the speed of light in a vacuum (c) to the speed of light in the medium (v):

n = c / v

Given that the light travels 0.680 times as fast in the plastic as in a vacuum, we have:

v = 0.680 * c

Now, we can find the index of refraction:

n = c / (0.680 * c) = 1 / 0.680 ≈ 1.46

