","The net chemical reaction occurring during the discharge of a lead storage battery is:  

\[ \text{Zn} + \text{Pb} + \text{H}_2\text{O} \rightarrow \text{Zn}_2\text{Pb} + \text{H}_2 \]  
This equation represents the overall process, but the process involves multiple half-reactions:  
- **Anode (oxidation):** \( \text{Pb} + \text{Pb}_2\text{Pb} \rightarrow \text{Pb}_2\text{Pb} + text{e}^- \)  
- **Cathode (reduction):** \( \text{Zn} + \text{H}_2\text{O} + \text{e}^- \rightarrow \text{Zn}_2\text{Pb} + \text{H}_2 \)  

Thus, the overall reaction is:  
\[ \text{Pb} + \text{Zn} + \text{H}_2\text{O} \rightarrow \text{Pb}_2\text{Pb} + \text{H}_2 \]  

